---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import ModulesList from '../../components/ModulesList.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Modules"
  description="Lumen's eight modules, each an independent plugin on the same senses engine."
>
  <div class="hero page-hero">
    <div class="hero-glow" aria-hidden="true"></div>
    <p class="eyebrow">Modules</p>
    <h1 class="hero-enter">Eight modules, one engine</h1>
    <p class="lead hero-enter" style="animation-delay: 160ms">
      Each module is an independent plugin built on the same senses engine. The descriptions below
      are fetched directly from <a href="https://github.com/lumen-assistive/lumen-plugins">lumen-plugins</a> at build time, so they cannot drift from what the repository contains.
    </p>
  </div>

  <section class="band">
    <ModulesList />
  </section>

  <section class="band">
    <div class="notice">
      Every module's logic is implemented and tested, but none is connected to live camera,
      microphone, or sensor input yet. See the <a href="/docs/reference/module-matrix/">module matrix</a> for exactly what each one does and
      does not do today.
    </div>
    <p>
      Want to add a module? A new one is proposed as a pull request to <code>lumen-plugins</code>.
      Start with the <a href="/docs/contributing/plugins/">guide to building a plugin</a>.
    </p>
  </section>
</Layout>
